<title>USA: Liposome to develop new cancer drug.</title>
<headline>Liposome to develop new cancer drug.</headline>
<dateline>PRINCETON, N.J. 1996-09-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Liposome Co Inc said on Tuesday it would launch a development program for ELL-12, a new cancer therapeutic that may have uses in treating cancers including prostate cancer and non small-cell lung carcinoma.</p>
<p>In preclinical studies conducted by Liposome scientists, ELL-12, a liposomal ether lipid, was shown to be active in mouse tumor models of melanoma, lung cancer and leukemia, the company said.</p>
<p>It has also been shown to be active in a model of human prostate cancer, it said.</p>
</text>
